requires pontif.shape.{Sphere, gradientField}

# docs/shapes.md S1 — the first SDF primitive, as its gradient field. `gradientField` samples the
# sphere's signed distance on a 24^3 grid and clamps it to a thin band around the surface, so a
# volumetric renderer lights the surface shell (tinted by gradient direction) rather than the whole
# box. For a crisp solid surface use `raymarch` instead (see render-sphere.ptf).
#
# The sampling is Pontif's; the result is a value. Nothing here draws.
main ( gradientField(Sphere(1.0)) )
